      "math_academy_id": "e-9684",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/7178cf6a642786f249a22cab09178eaa62e63e47a4e3bb28969ca90f4d97db95.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the distances some athletes in a sports club cover during a training session, and the time (in minutes) it takes. Use the trend line to estimate how long it takes a club athlete to run $10$ km.",
      "worked_solution": "To make our estimation, we proceed as follows:\n\n- We start at $y=10$ on the vertical axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/c595c42406bbf7ad4d71b6ceb9914b839f529b26135c467231a38b3cc48223c8.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/28f757380ba22cddc96fbd382578a6b8dc9bba258adfec704413047e73d54c93.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the horizontal axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14227574/assets/85754fb62bbee8c597a71ad8fe30e5eabca3ed9c6304b1832e14788b1e809bcd.png)\n\nTherefore, a club athlete can run $10$ kilometers in approximately $45$ minutes.",
